
# Real data-center data stays on this machine: only the simulations (sim_*) may go to GitHub.
# Everything else under app/data (the real data sets, the machine-local _local/ folder,
# and the models, graphs, sites and backups built from them) is never committed.
# This includes the user's components (app/data/_components/, Heat Distribution › Components): fitted ones carry
# numbers learned from the user's data.
app/data/*
!app/data/sim_*/
# The Site map's heat demand: the built files of the Wärmeatlas Hessen (the owner's decision; © LEA, no open
# licence: never in a public copy) and of NRW (dl-de/zero-2.0) are shared; the downloads they come from are not.
!app/data/_external/
app/data/_external/*/*
!app/data/_external/waermeatlas/buildings.sqlite
!app/data/_external/nrw/buildings.sqlite
app/data/*/.backup/
# P&ID drawings put into the app (may be confidential), also in simulation folders
app/data/*/pid.png
app/data/*/pid_plant.json
app/data/*/pid_construct.json
app/data/*/pid_views/
# derived Open-Meteo temperatures (app/backend/core/weather.py): never committed, also not for simulations
app/data/*/weather_open_meteo.json
# Shared data versions: a per-machine symlink to the user's data folder (app/scripts/link-data.sh), and the
# version chosen last on this machine. No trailing slash: a slash-only pattern does not match a symlink.
app/data_versions
app/.data_version

# graphify knowledge graph of the code (generated: /graphify app_idz)
graphify-out/

# Generated by a build, a docs build or a test run: never tracked (start.sh builds the page when web/dist is missing)
docs/_build/
app/web/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
test-results/
playwright-report/
# the saved project states of a data center (app/data/_status/<dc>/, one file per save), not an example
app/data/_status/

# what the app makes from an example (prepared variables, aggregated files, their recipe): never committed
app/data/*/silver/

# The lock file is tracked (CI's `uv sync --frozen` needs it), although the enclosing repository ignores uv.lock
!app/uv.lock

# Research notes and reports on outside data sources (kept locally, not part of the app)
reports/
research_notes/
